  "title": "Subject element schema",
  "description": "\nStructured information on a subject.\n\nArgs\n----\nbiological_sex : ~openminds.latest.controlled_terms.biological_sex.BiologicalSex\n    Differentiation of individuals of most species (animals and plants) based on the type of gametes they produce.\ninternal_identifier : str\n    Term or code that identifies the subject within a particular product.\nis_part_of : ~openminds.latest.core.research.subject_group.SubjectGroup\n    Reference to the ensemble of multiple things or beings.\nlookup_label : str\n    no description available\nspecies : ~openminds.latest.controlled_terms.species.Species, ~openminds.latest.core.research.strain.Strain\n    Category of biological classification comprising related organisms or populations potentially capable of interbreeding, and being designated by a binomial that consists of the name of a genus followed by a Latin or latinized uncapitalized noun or adjective.\nstudied_states : ~openminds.latest.core.research.subject_state.SubjectState\n    Reference to a point in time at which the subject was studied in a particular mode or condition.\n\n",
